; Dependency policy (see "Dependency install policy" in README.md):
;
; - Dependencies are installed from package-lock.json with `npm ci`.
;   npm 11 resolves version ranges through a release-age filter
;   (`--before` / `min-release-age`), and the npm wrapper on Lumi dev
;   machines injects a 7-day window into every install. Fresh
;   resolution of a dependency published in the last few days fails
;   with ETARGET, so ranges must never be re-resolved implicitly.
; - CLI flags (including the injected --before) take precedence over
;   this file, so an .npmrc override cannot beat the wrapper. Lockfile
;   discipline is the actual immunity.
;
; save-exact keeps every new dependency pinned to an exact version so
; lockfile diffs stay reviewable and ranges never widen silently.
save-exact=true
